<item>
            <title>[LU-20609] FIEMAP on a sparse DoM file makes every later write to that file stall</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20609</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Reproduction&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
### client A - sparse DoM file
mkdir /mnt/lustre/dom
lfs setstripe -E 1M -L mdt -E -1 -c 1 /mnt/lustre/dom
dd &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;=/dev/zero of=/mnt/lustre/dom/f1 bs=4k count=1 seek=32 &#160; &#160; # hole 0..128K

### client B - write it and keep it open, so B holds the DOM lock
/usr/lib64/lustre/tests/multiop /mnt/lustre/dom/f1 Ow_ &amp;amp;

### client A - one FIEMAP with FIEMAP_FLAG_SYNC; returns correct extents
/usr/lib64/lustre/tests/checkfiemap /mnt/lustre/dom/f1 4096

### client A - any write to that file from now on
dd &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;=/dev/zero of=/mnt/lustre/dom/f1 bs=4k count=1 conv=notrunc # stall!&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Found by graph-hunter-v1&lt;/p&gt;</description>
